meta {
  name: 00 READ ME first
  type: http
  seq: 0
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Training (not Exam Day) — one request chain that proves each CEFR level
  can open its practice paper on the existing skill routes.

  WHAT THIS CHECKS
  A1 MT 9 and A2 MT 8: Lesen + Hören; A1 also training play ×2 (re-grant).
  B1: catalogue (of-the-week only, no Prep Pass) then Lesen, Hören,
  training play ×2 when that paper has audio_url, Sprachbausteine, Schreiben.
  B2 MT 7: Lesen, Hören, Sprachbausteine, Schreiben (B-family shapes).
  Wrong-level refusal: A1 student cannot open a B2 paper.

  Deeper A1/A2 submit scoring (Lösungsschlüssel / UNRECOGNISED) stays in
  `bruno/A1 Level` and `bruno/A2 Level` P01–P04. This folder is the
  per-level smoke matrix.

  BEFORE YOU START
  1. `node -r ./scripts/env-test-first.cjs scripts/seed-b2-bruno-fixture.mjs`
     Must print ep-misty-sea and A1/A2/B2 papers.
  2. `npm run start:testdb`
  3. Center Auth / 03 Login (sets {{accessToken}} for the B2 seat PATCH).

  ORDER
  Run in seq. A1/A2/B1 seats already carry their level in the fixture.
  B2 needs 40 (set seat level) then 41–42 (login + redeem).

  RE-RUNNING
  Seat redeem is 409 if already claimed — re-run the fixture script.
}
